## Final answer of writer
I fixed the paging bug in `src/paginate.js`. When the item count was an exact multiple of the page size, the last page came back empty instead of holding the last full page of items.

The cause was that the last page's length was computed as `items.length % size`, which is 0 in that case. I removed that calculation and now take `items.slice(start, start + size)` for every page. `slice` stops at the end of the array, so a partial last page still holds the leftover items.

`npm test` now passes all 4 tests, including the existing multiple-of-page-size case, which was failing before. I created no scratch files. `git status` shows only `src/paginate.js` modified.

